---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Rent Increase Advisory" description="Know if your rent increase is legal under Act 220, how much you can increase, and the proper notice procedure.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="/services/" style="color:#516784; text-decoration:none; margin-bottom:1rem; display:inline-block;">← Back to Services</a>

      <h1>Rent Increase Advisory</h1>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width:680px; margin-bottom:2rem;">Written guidance on whether a proposed rent increase is lawful, how much you're allowed to increase, and the correct notice procedure under Act 220.</p>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f0f4f8; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Why You Need This Service</h2>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;">Many landlords lose rent disputes because they increase rent incorrectly. Common mistakes:</p>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8; margin:1.5rem 0;">
          <li><strong>Timing:</strong> You can't increase in the first year, or you increase at the wrong point in the lease</li>
          <li><strong>Amount:</strong> You increase more than Act 220 allows</li>
          <li><strong>Notice:</strong> You don't give proper written notice, or the notice is incomplete</li>
          <li><strong>Justification:</strong> You don't explain why the increase is reasonable</li>
          <li><strong>Timing of Service:</strong> You don't give the required notice period (usually 3 months)</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;"><strong>This service gives you a legal roadmap for increasing rent without ending up in dispute.</strong></p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">What We Cover</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li><strong>Eligibility:</strong> Can you legally increase rent right now?</li>
          <li><strong>Timing:</strong> When is the earliest you can increase?</li>
          <li><strong>Amount:</strong> How much can you legally increase?</li>
          <li><strong>Notice Period:</strong> How much notice must you give?</li>
          <li><strong>Justification:</strong> What reasons support the increase?</li>
          <li><strong>Notice Language:</strong> What to write in the increase notice</li>
          <li><strong>Service Method:</strong> How to serve the notice correctly</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">What You Get</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li><strong>Written Advice:</strong> Yes/no on whether you can increase, and by how much</li>
          <li><strong>Timing Guidance:</strong> Exact date you're allowed to increase</li>
          <li><strong>Notice Template:</strong> Ready-to-use language for your increase notice</li>
          <li><strong>Act 220 Reference:</strong> Which provisions support your position</li>
          <li><strong>Defensibility:</strong> Documentation showing the increase is lawful</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#fff3cd; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">When You Need This Service</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li>You're approaching the end of year one and want to know if you can increase</li>
          <li>You've held a property for several years and want to raise rent</li>
          <li>You've improved the property and want to justify a larger increase</li>
          <li>A tenant has already rejected your increase and you want to know your position</li>
          <li>You want to be sure you're following the law before serving notice</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#e8f4f8; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">The Risk of Getting It Wrong</h2>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;">An improper rent increase notice can be challenged at Rent Control. The magistrate might:</p>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8; margin:1rem 0;">
          <li>Reject your increase entirely</li>
          <li>Allow only a smaller increase</li>
          <li>Order you to refund overcharges</li>
          <li>Rule that your notice was invalid</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;"><strong>GHS 250 in advice now prevents months of dispute and lost rent.</strong></p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Pricing & Turnaround</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.2rem; font-weight:700; color:#516784; margin:0;">GHS 250</p>
        <p style="color:#666; margin:0.5rem 0;">One fixed price for complete advisory</p>
        <p style="font-weight:600; margin-top:1rem;">Turnaround: 2 working days</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:3rem 0; text-align:center;">
        <a href="/services/" style="display:inline-block; padding:1rem 2rem; background:#516784; color:white; text-decoration:none; border-radius:4px; font-weight:600; margin-right:1rem;">Request a Quote</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/233208071633" style="display:inline-block; padding:1rem 2rem; background:#f0f4f8; color:#516784; text-decoration:none; border-radius:4px; font-weight:600; border:1px solid #516784;">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
